`unescape_html` in `escapes/catalog.py` is complete and correct; the `ENTITIES` table was left untouched and no code changes were required. It uses one compiled pattern (`&(#(?:[xX][0-9a-fA-F]+|[0-9]+)|[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*);`) plus a single `re.sub` pass, so:

- named references decode case-sensitively from `ENTITIES` (`&eacute;`→é, `&lt;p&gt;`→`<p>`, `&AElig;`/`&aelig;` differ, `&AMP;` stays literal);
- numeric references decode as decimal (`&#65;`→A) and hex in either case (`&#x4a;`→J, `&#X10ffff;`→U+10FFFF);
- unknown names and malformed references are left unchanged;
- replacement text is never rescanned (`&#38;amp;`→`&amp;`, `&amp;amp;`→`&amp;`, `&#38;#65;`→`&#65;`).

